    "math_academy_id": "q-43339",
    "knowledge_point_id": "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7",
    "knowledge_point": "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/85b13f2236c5f00da34ea71fdbfc967882fa6e66c347f6ef40c0604391a5d68e.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $m∠A.$",
    "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{15}{30} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
